# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Build-time environment. `apps/game/.env.production` carries the GA measurement
# id for a deploy run from a developer's machine; in Workers Builds the same
# variable is set as a build variable in Cloudflare. Neither is a secret — the id
# ships in the bundle and is readable in any request — but this repository is
# public, and an id committed here is an id every fork measures into.
# `apps/game/.env.example` is the committed documentation of what may be set.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/README.md
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Astro's generated types. `astro sync` writes them; they describe this
# checkout's pages rather than the source that produces them.
apps/game/.astro/

# InertialRef
.tsbuildinfo
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
.vitest

# Claude Code. `.claude/settings.json`, `rules/`, `skills/`, `agents/` and `hooks/` are
# committed on purpose — they are the project's configuration, not a developer's. These
# four are not:
#
#   worktrees/          parallel checkouts; git already tracks them as worktrees, and a
#                       committed one would be a repository inside a repository
#   settings.local.json personal overrides, including permission approvals Claude writes
#   .cache/             the Stop gate's per-session markers
#   agent-memory-local/ subagent memory scoped `local` rather than `project`
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.cache/
.claude/agent-memory-local/

# Raw catalogue downloads. 34 MB of HYG to produce a 460 KB asset, and the asset
# is what the game needs — `pnpm catalog:fetch` re-downloads them, and
# `data/catalog/manifest.json` records the digest of exactly what was used.
.data/

# Throwaway probes. The cutscene work is an iterate-against-a-measurement
# loop, and the cheap half of it is a Node script that samples the director and
# prints geometry — written, read once, and thrown away. They are not source
# and must not be committed.
.scratch/

# The documentation site's staged content: seventy markdown files and the whole
# of `packages/*` rendered to JSON that the client fetches at runtime.
# `pnpm docs:build` writes it and `pnpm build` runs that first, so a deploy always
# carries it; it is derived from files in this repository and committing it
# would be committing a second copy of the documentation that drifts from the
# first. `scripts/docs/build.mjs` explains where it goes and why.
apps/game/public/doc-content/

# Media the build pulls out of the site's own R2 bucket rather than carrying —
# today, the reference edit's audio track. A local copy of copyrighted music
# whose use here is a fair-use claim this project is willing to make in a
# deployment and not in a git history, which is permanent and mirrored by every
# fork. `pnpm media:pull` fetches it, `scripts/media.mjs` explains the whole
# arrangement, and the overlay plays the scene silent when it is absent.
#
# Ignored as a directory, not as a filename: the next thing that has to arrive
# this way should not need a second rule and a second thing to remember.
apps/game/public/media/
